    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a45f9889d5006a6c0384",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Michael Durbin",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a45f9889d5006a6c0384",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Indeed... one in the same.</p>\n\n<p>The trouble is, since we can export from any point, we don't know if non-exported parent (ancestor) nodes are real nodes or not.  Perhaps we should force the exporter to include the RDF for any ancestor nodes of exported nodes and then import all the nodes in a breadth-first fashion (or at least guarantee to import parents before children).</p>",
     "created": "09/Sep/16 3:04 PM",
     "id": "17481",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12155/comment/17481",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a45f9889d5006a6c0384",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
